Current list of drivers to be implemented and the status of re-implementation
=====================================================

Guest packaging (`rbuild kernel` / `rbuild kerneldrivers` on the ppc build box)
is tracked separately from reconstruction completeness. Paths listed in
`src/rbuild-1/kernel-drivers-blacklist.json` are skipped until they package;
remove an entry there to promote a driver into the optional driver pass.

bus
 * drvPExpert - packaged as drvpexpert-29.apk (kernel core); not yet hardware-tested
 * drvPPCOHare - packaged as drvppcohare-2.apk; copy of
   src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvOHare; see tools/ppc_package_check.py; not yet
   hardware-tested

ide
 * drvPPCSwimFloppy - blacklisted WIP; needs compile and then test

input
 * drvPPCSerialPort - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPPCCuda - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvCuda; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCPMU - copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvPMU; see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvIOADBDevice - blacklisted WIP; STUB, no in-tree source; class/selector list
   scaffolded from the shipped binary, every method body empty

network
 * drvPPCGem - blacklisted WIP; needs compile and then test
 * drvPPCGNic - blacklisted WIP; needs compile and then test
 * drvPPCBMac - packaged as drvppcbmac-2.apk; copy of
   src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvBMacEnet; see tools/ppc_package_check.py; not yet
   hardware-tested
 * drvPPCMace - blacklisted WIP; copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvMaceEnet;
   see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCDec21040 - packaged as drvppcdec21040-2.apk; copy of
   src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvDECchip21040; see tools/ppc_package_check.py;
   not yet hardware-tested
 * drvDEC21x4Ethernet - blacklisted WIP; STUB, no in-tree source; class/selector
   list scaffolded from the shipped binary, every method body empty

scsi
 * drvPPC53c96 - blacklisted WIP; copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvApple96_SCSI;
   see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCMesh - blacklisted WIP; copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvAppleMesh_SCSI;
   see tools/ppc_package_check.py
 * drvPPCSym8xx - blacklisted WIP; copy of src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/drvSymbios8xx;
   see tools/ppc_package_check.py

sound
 * drvPPCAwacs - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPPCBurgundy - blacklisted WIP; needs compile and then test
 * drvPPCTASAudio - blacklisted WIP; needs compile and then test

video

Nine of the entries above marked "copy of ..." are byte-identical copies of the
sources they cite, which also still live under src/kernel-7/bsd/dev/ppc/ and
build into the kernel via conf/files.ppc; the two copies are not kept in sync
automatically. Run tools/ppc_package_check.py to check whether they have
drifted apart.

The two entries marked STUB have no implementation at all: their headers and
.m files declare every selector the shipped binary carries, with empty
method bodies, so a later reconstruction has a starting point.
